    {
        "id": "ch8_2_2-1",
        "text": "Creating new directories\nYou can use the graphical interface in Files to create a new directory. Just follow\nthese steps:\n1. Browse to the directory you want to create the directory in.\nYou need to have the directory open and be inside its window before\nproceeding.\n2. Right-click an empty spot inside that directory.\nMake sure that you didn\u2019t highlight anything in the directory. A context menu\nappears.\n3. Choose New Folder.\nA new directory icon appears, highlighted, and with the name open for editing.\n4. Type the name you want to assign to this directory and then click Create.\nThe name is assigned to the directory.\nThat\u2019s a lot easier than messing around with the cryptic mkdir command in the\ncommand line!",
